ombined pandoc output) and degrades the entire safe-run segment to verbatim Markdown on a preservation miss — not just on timeout/non-zero exit — so ADR 0095 invariant #1 is preserved at the new run granularity.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"indeterminate","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'On a safe-run call's timeout or non-zero exit, degrade that entire safe-run segment to its original Markdown verbatim' — no mention of the code-fragment preservation check.","Landed code wiki_render.py:381-389: `_render_unit` computes `code_fragments(text)` and returns the source verbatim on any fragment that fails to reappear in order (reason='preservation_failure').","ADR 0095 invariant #1: 'every code fragment of the source must reappear byte-identically and in order, or that unit falls back to its original Markdown' — the property that makes the renderer non-corrupting.","Module docstring lines 14-16: 'A unit that cannot convert losslessly is never converted, which is what makes the renderer non-corrupting rather than merely lossy.'"],"finding":"The batch/segment fallback specifies only timeout and non-zero-exit as degrade triggers, omitting the landed renderer's load-bearing per-unit code-fragment PRESERVATION check (ADR 0095 invariant #1, _render_unit lines 381-389), which must be re-applied at the run/segment granularity or the non-corruption guarantee is silently lost when a batch converts with exit 0 but escapes a code fragment.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f90e310dab6d26496","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > 'Hard timeout + ... verbatim fallback'; AC line 1 ('on timeout or non-zero exit it degrades that safe-run segment')","norm_id":"nc942fc53e27f081b","priority":1.0,"reason":"prerequisite-coverage-indeterminate","scenarios":["A safe run containing an inline-code span whose punctuation pandoc escapes (e.g. `` `->` `` -> `{{\\->}}`) converts with exit 0 and no timeout; with only timeout/exit-code triggers the corrupted wiki is emitted, dropping invariant #1.","A run where one unit's fragment is preserved but another's is not — must the WHOLE segment fall back, or is verification per-fragment over the combined output? The plan does not say."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add preservation-failure to the segment-level fallback triggers: after a successful (exit-0, non-timed-out) batch conversion, verify the ordered concatenation of code_fragments() for every render unit in the run reappears in the combined wiki output, and on any miss degrade that whole safe-run segment to its original Markdown (segment == fallback boundary, exactly as for timeout/non-zero exit), with a segment-level fallback marker.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the process-group reaping (start_new_session=True + killpg via reap_process_group) behaves on Windows, or scope the reaping guarantee to POSIX platforms and note the fallback there.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'builds its OWN subprocess.Popen([pandoc_path, …], start_new_session=True) ... passes that Popen to the leaf rebar._proc.reap_process_group ... killpg SIGTERM→grace→SIGKILL→bounded drain'","Platform fact: os.killpg and process-group signalling are POSIX-only; on CPython/Windows os.killpg is unavailable and start_new_session has no effect, so the SIGTERM/SIGKILL killpg drain the plan depends on to reap the pathological grandchild cannot run.","Matrix cell: Windows is a supported Platform-and-venue; rebar must run identically as a Python library / CLI / MCP there."],"finding":"The plan explicitly introduces subprocess.Popen(start_new_session=True) plus process-group reaping (killpg SIGTERM/SIGKILL via reap_process_group) directly in wiki_render.py, but does not address the Windows platform where os.killpg / process groups do not exist and start_new_session is a no-op, so the CPU-spinning grandchild reaping the plan relies on cannot occur.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c686c3f49ad9d9d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Hard timeout + process-group reaping'; Scope — 'own subprocess.Popen(start_new_session=True) ... rebar._proc.reap_process_group'","norm_id":"nf1c93cb94699762d","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["Windows developer workstation or Windows CI runner: a pathological DC field drives the pandoc jira reader to spin; the timeout fires but reap_process_group's killpg path raises/no-ops, so the grandchild is orphaned and keeps burning CPU — the exact hazard this story exists to close remains open on Windows."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence noting reap_process_group's cross-platform contract (as already used by the ACLI transport) covers Windows, or explicitly bound the killpg reaping to POSIX and describe the Windo